From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:01:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Interpolate GLSL pixel shader inputs where D3D does.

Inputs to be interpolated at the centroid or at the sample were
interpolated at the pixel's centre, with a FIXME for each; and in a shader
run for each sample, the other inputs were interpolated at the sample,
where D3D keeps them at the centre (measured on Windows with wine-altars'
tools/d3d11sampleprobe).

Centroid and sample are auxiliary qualifiers, which from GLSL 4.40 on
still have to match between the stages' interface blocks while vertex
shaders are not compiled for the pixel shader's interpolation modes; so
neither is declared, and the pixel shader takes such an input with
interpolateAtCentroid() or interpolateAtSample(..., gl_SampleID), and in a
shader run per sample, a plain one with interpolateAtOffset(..., 0).

The test draws with a shader that reads the sample index and one with an
input interpolated at the sample, compiled by Windows' compiler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b6df68716f30930e46818579df810f3bb834427a)

